// Sear is picked over Stab/Slash/Bash for its built-in Burning rider
// (common/src/comp/melee.rs), which fits "emerald fire erupts from the
// wound" directly -- the best flavor match of the four MeleeConstructorKind
// options available for a melee spell (see booming_blade.ron for why none
// of them offer a real elemental damage_kind field; Sear's own hardcoded
// kind is Energy, not Fire, but at least it is a magical kind rather than a
// physical one).
//
// The "flame leaps to a second nearby foe" rider is modeled with
// `multi_target: Some(Normal)`, the same wide-swing-hits-everyone-in-arc
// primitive sword cleave abilities use (see
// assets/common/abilities/sword/cleaving_cross_cut.ron) -- both targets take
// equal power, which is the closest existing analogue to "the second target
// also takes the secondary fire damage." Per-target damage is halved
// relative to a single-target cantrip (eldritch_blast.ron in this same
// folder applies the same discipline for its own multi-hit cantrip, split
// 8+8 instead of one shot at full cantrip damage) so hitting both targets
// totals to roughly one single-target cantrip's worth of damage, not double.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Sear(damage: 8, poise: 5, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 80.0,
        multi_target: Some(Normal),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
